0.8 = 25.875 → 25.875 tasks/s. Remaining two servers give 20 → need 5.875 tasks/s more → ~6 tasks/s, i.e. one more server of 10 tasks/s (total 3 surviving = 30 → but wait, after failure of one, if we have 4 total servers, 3 remain = 30 tasks/s, ρ = 20.7/30 = 69%). Or partial: 6 tasks/s ≈ 60% of a server. So minimum: +6 tasks/s (e.g. one additional server of 10 tasks/s, or 60% capacity top-up). If we keep 80% threshold strictly: +5.875 tasks/s.\n\nAlso must consider capacity needed to keep threshold at 80%: with N servers of 10: need 10N ≥ 25.875 → N ≥ 2.5875 → 3 surviving servers → 4 total. So add 1 server (4 × 10 = 40; after failure 30 → ρ = 69%).\n\nLet me also double-check the \"10 задач/с\" as capacity ceiling including service concurrency: server handles 10 tasks/s with 0.08s each → needs 0.8 concurrent workers. So servers presumably have limited parallelism; capacity 10/s is the constraint. Fine.\n\nAlso note: at ρ = 103.5% queue grows without bound: 20.7 − 20 = 0.7 tasks/s backlog accumulates; latency unbounded. Little's law with overload: L grows linearly, W = L/λ → unbounded.\n\nLet me write numbers precisely:\n- Before: 18/30 = 0.6; 1.44/2.4 = 0.6.\n- After: 20.7/20 = 1.035.\n- Concurrency: 1.44 before, 1.656 needed after vs 1.6 available; deficit 0.056 concurrent ≈ equivalent 0.7 tasks/s.\n- Backlog growth: 0.7 tasks/s → after 60 s, 42 tasks queued.\n\nMinimal extra: 5.875 tasks/s ≈ 6 tasks/s for 80% target; 0.7 tasks/s would only reach 100% (critical, no margin) — not acceptable; for 100% exactly need +0.7.\n\nJSON single object.\n\nFormat: 8-12 lines итог. Let me structure:\n\nConfirmation line first (canon). Then numbers. Then JSON.\n\nKeep it compact. The JSON should be single object. Include fields: before{...}, after{...}, little, threshold, extra_capacity, verdict.\n\nI'll write in Russian.\n\nLines: I'll aim for ≤12 lines of prose bullet points.\n\nNote: \"Вариант проверки: single-json\" — I'll put JSON as one line (single-line JSON) so it's a single JSON object on one line. Good.\n\nCompute 15% extra: 18 * 1.15 = 20.7 ✓.\n\nRequired capacity at 80%: 20.7 * 0.08 / 0.8 = 1.656/0.8 = 2.07 erlangs → /0.08 = 25.875 tasks/s ✓. Equivalent servers: 25.875/10 = 2.5875 → 3 servers surviving → 4 total.\n\nCheck headroom multiplier before: 0.8 threshold → max λ = 24 tasks/s; current 18 → 33% growth room.\n\nAfter failure without retries: 18/20 = 90% — already above 80%.\n\nWrite it.\n\nAlso should I include JIRA? block? Not a work task (question, computation). No.\n\nGate marker? No file changes. Not needed.\n\nLet me write the answer."
